E4 SLO outbox value-byte bounded scan
Date: 2026-10-05

Change:
- SloObservationOutboxStore.scan now visits the META key range through ShardStore.visitResult rather than materializing the whole record-limited page before checking its byte allowance.
- The scan uses a value-only BoundedReadBudget to preserve its existing contract: maxBytes counts encoded ValueEnvelope bytes, not the fixed key. ShardStore's finite-byte iterator path obtains a value length before requesting the full Java array. A later record that does not fit leaves the already completed prefix for the next export turn; a first record larger than the allowance fails closed.
- A real RocksDB regression stores two same-sized Starts and sets the page limit one byte below their combined encoded value size; scan returns the first Start only. Existing exact-fit and first-record-too-large cases remain covered.

